`KdevA4plusBound`: the crude `j(τ)²`-estimate gives only `O(‖q(τ)‖^{-1})`, so the
`Δ(τ)j(τ)² = E₄(τ)³j(τ)`-monomials must be shown to cancel against the `j(τ)¹`- and
`j(τ)⁰`-monomials (numerically the `k = 4` coefficient is `O(1)` up to `scale`-powers). -/
def Bracket24B4Bound (ℓ : Work.Kernels.LogLambdaData) : Prop :=
  ∃ C N M : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ 0 ≤ N ∧ 0 ≤ M ∧
    ∀ (τ z : UpperHalfPlane) (t : ℝ), Work.Asymptotics.Funnel τ → τ.im + 1 ≤ t →
      0 ≤ z.re → z.re ≤ 1 → z.im = t →
      ‖Bracket24B4 ℓ τ z‖ ≤ C * (Work.Kernels.scale τ) ^ N * (1 + t) ^ M

/-- **The `E(z)^6`-coefficient bound** (the crude `O(‖q(τ)‖^{-1})`, which is exactly the
strength the tail bound needs at `k = 6`). -/
def Bracket24B6Bound (ℓ : Work.Kernels.LogLambdaData) : Prop :=
  ∃ C N M : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ 0 ≤ N ∧ 0 ≤ M ∧
    ∀ (τ z : UpperHalfPlane) (t : ℝ), Work.Asymptotics.Funnel τ → τ.im + 1 ≤ t →
      0 ≤ z.re → z.re ≤ 1 → z.im = t →
      ‖Bracket24B6 ℓ τ z‖
        ≤ C * (‖Work.Kernels.qParamFun τ‖)⁻¹ * (Work.Kernels.scale τ) ^ N * (1 + t) ^ M

/-- **The `E(z)^7`-coefficient bound** (crude `O(‖q(τ)‖^{-1})`; the tail bound needs only
`‖q(τ)‖^{-3/2}`, which is weaker since `‖q(τ)‖ ≤ 1`). -/
def Bracket24B7Bound (ℓ : Work.Kernels.LogLambdaData) : Prop :=
  ∃ C N M : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ 0 ≤ N ∧ 0 ≤ M ∧
    ∀ (τ z : UpperHalfPlane) (t : ℝ), Work.Asymptotics.Funnel τ → τ.im + 1 ≤ t →
      0 ≤ z.re → z.re ≤ 1 → z.im = t →
      ‖Bracket24B7 ℓ τ z‖
        ≤ C * (‖Work.Kernels.qParamFun τ‖)⁻¹ * (Work.Kernels.scale τ) ^ N * (1 + t) ^ M

end

end Work.Asymptotics.KhatE1Core
